# Where "Landing" in the nav points while developing.
#
# Nowhere special anymore, and that is the point: the unified dev server
# (`npm run dev`, tools/dev-all.mjs) serves this app under /app/ and the landing
# page at / on the SAME origin, which is the exact arrangement landingHref()'s
# fallback of "/" was written for. An override here can only point somewhere
# worse - the old one pointed at the retired port 5175 and outlived the server
# that listened there.
#
# Committed on purpose, comment and all, so the next developer finds the
# reasoning instead of rediscovering the override.
#
# VITE_LANDING_URL is only needed for a deployment that serves the landing page
# on a DIFFERENT origin than the app.
